      "evidence_id": "EV_012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "speaker_role": "doctor",
      "transcript_text": "Medical history?",
      "start_timestamp": "01:50",
      "end_timestamp": "01:51",
      "supports": [
        "medical_history.past_medical_history[0]",
        "medical_history.past_medical_history[1]",
        "medical_history.past_medical_history[2]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "speaker_role": "patient",
      "transcript_text": "High cholesterol, anaemia, a few years back, and I had a stomach problem, a bit of coeliac, they said, but they weren't sure.",
      "start_timestamp": "01:55",
      "end_timestamp": "02:07",
      "supports": [
        "medical_history.past_medical_history[0]",
        "medical_history.past_medical_history[1]",
        "medical_history.past_medical_history[2]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "speaker_role": "doctor",
      "transcript_text": "Pulse 70, temperature 36.6.",
      "start_timestamp": "02:35",
      "end_timestamp": "02:38",
      "supports": [
        "vital_signs[0]",
        "vital_signs[1]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_015",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "speaker_role": "doctor",
      "transcript_text": "Yes, a minor aphthous ulcer. The picture of recurrent ulcers in someone with a history of anaemia and possible coeliac makes me want to look for a nutritional cause.",
      "start_timestamp": "03:35",
      "end_timestamp": "03:49",
      "supports": [
        "clinical_assessment[0]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "speaker_role": "doctor",
      "transcript_text": "Low iron, B12 or folate, or coeliac disease, can all make ulcers recur. I'd like to arrange a blood test for these, and a coeliac screen.",
      "start_timestamp": "03:59",
      "end_timestamp": "04:13",
      "supports": [
        "procedures_and_investigations[0]",
        "clinical_actions[0]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_017",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "speaker_role": "doctor",
      "transcript_text": "In the meantime, avoid spicy, acidic and crunchy foods, brush with a soft brush, and use a toothpaste without sodium lauryl sulphate.",
      "start_timestamp": "04:22",
      "end_timestamp": "04:33",
      "supports": [
        "clinical_actions[2]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "speaker_role": "doctor",
